  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "n_overview",
      "content": "# Medusa returns\nA customer or merchant opens a return, the warehouse receives and inspects the items, then a refund is issued through Stripe. See the [Medusa return docs](https://docs.medusajs.com/) for the underlying data model.",
      "color": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "id": "n_ship",
      "content": "## Return shipping\nMedusa generates the **return label**, the customer ships the parcel back, and the warehouse logs receipt before inspection.",
      "attachTo": ["g_ship"],
      "color": "blue",
      "layers": ["business"]
    },
    {
      "id": "n_inspection",
      "content": "## Inspection\nItems are checked by hand against the original order line. Notes:\n- condition, not just quantity\n- photos attached to the return record\n- `inspect` decides the outcome",
      "attachTo": ["receive", "inspect"],
      "color": "green",
      "layers": ["business"]
    },
    {
      "id": "n_refund_cap",
      "content": "**Refund exceeds cap** halts the flow — a merchant must approve any refund over the configured limit before Stripe is called.",
      "attachTo": ["refund_check"],
      "color": "red",
      "layers": ["edge"]
    }
  ]
